    content: "<p>Wondering how to scan a WiFi QR code without manually entering a password? Simply open your phone's camera, point it at the QR code, and tap the WiFi connection prompt. Your phone can then connect using the network details stored in the code.</p>\n<p>This works on many modern Android phones and iPhones. Here's how to do it on each device.</p>\n<h2>How to Scan a WiFi QR Code: Quick Steps</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Turn on WiFi on your phone.</li>\n<li>Open your phone's Camera app.</li>\n<li>Point the camera at the WiFi QR code.</li>\n<li>Keep the entire code visible on the screen.</li>\n<li>Tap the WiFi network prompt when it appears.</li>\n<li>Confirm the connection.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Once connected, check your phone's WiFi settings to make sure it joined the correct network.</p>\n<h2>How to Scan a WiFi QR Code on Android</h2>\n<p>Most modern Android phones support QR code scanning through the camera or a built-in scanner.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Open the Camera app.</li>\n<li>Point it toward the WiFi QR code.</li>\n<li>Wait for the network connection option to appear.</li>\n<li>Tap the prompt to join the network.</li>\n<li>Confirm that WiFi is connected.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>If your camera doesn't recognize the code, open your phone's Quick Settings panel and look for Scan QR Code.</p>\n<p>You can also try Google Lens if it's available on your device.</p>\n<p>The exact steps may vary between Samsung, Google Pixel, Xiaomi, and other Android phones.</p>\n<h2>How to Scan a WiFi QR Code on iPhone</h2>\n<p>You can connect to a compatible WiFi network using your iPhone's built-in camera.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Open the Camera app.</li>\n<li>Position the WiFi QR code inside the camera frame.</li>\n<li>Wait for the connection notification.</li>\n<li>Tap the prompt to join the WiFi network.</li>\n<li>Confirm the connection if asked.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>You can also use the Scan Code option in the Control Center.</p>\n<p>You normally don't need to install a separate QR scanner app.</p>\n<h2>How to Scan a WiFi QR Code From a Screenshot</h2>\n<p>If someone sends you a WiFi QR code as an image, you may be able to scan it without printing it.</p>\n<p>On supported phones:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Save the QR code image.</li>\n<li>Open it in your phone's photo gallery.</li>\n<li>Use the available QR recognition feature, such as Google Lens or Live Text on supported iPhones.</li>\n<li>Select the WiFi connection option if one appears.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>If your phone cannot recognize the saved image, display it on another device and scan it using your phone's camera.</p>\n<h2>Why Is My WiFi QR Code Not Scanning?</h2>\n<p>If your phone doesn't recognize the QR code or fails to connect, check the following problems.</p>\n<h3>The Camera Cannot Read the Code</h3>\n<p>Make sure the QR code is clearly visible. Increase the screen brightness, improve the lighting, and keep the camera steady.</p>\n<h3>The WiFi Password Has Changed</h3>\n<p>A QR code containing an old password may scan correctly but fail to connect.</p>\n<p>Ask the network owner for an updated code.</p>\n<h3>The Network Is Out of Range</h3>\n<p>Your phone must be within range of the WiFi network. Move closer to the router and try again.</p>\n<h3>The QR Code Contains Incorrect Details</h3>\n<p>The network name, password, or security setting may have been entered incorrectly when the code was created.</p>\n<p>The network owner should check those details and generate a corrected QR code.</p>\n<h2>How to Create a WiFi QR Code for Others to Scan</h2>\n<p>If you want friends, family, or guests to connect to your WiFi without typing the password, you can create a QR code for your network.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Open the <a href=\"/wifi-qr-code-generator/\">free WiFi QR Code Generator</a>.</li>\n<li>Enter your WiFi network name (SSID).</li>\n<li>Select the correct security type.</li>\n<li>Enter your WiFi password.</li>\n<li>Generate the QR code.</li>\n<li>Download it or display it on your screen.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Test the code with another phone before sharing it.</p>\n<p class=\"blog-callout\"><strong>Security tip:</strong> A WiFi QR code contains network credentials that may be decoded. Use a guest network when sharing WiFi access with visitors.</p>\n<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\n<h3>Can I scan a WiFi QR code without a password?</h3>\n<p>Yes. A compatible phone can read the password stored in the QR code and offer to connect without requiring you to type it.</p>\n<h3>Do I need an app to scan a WiFi QR code?</h3>\n<p>Usually not. Many Android phones and iPhones can scan QR codes using their built-in camera or QR scanner.</p>\n<h3>Can an iPhone scan an Android WiFi QR code?</h3>\n<p>Yes. An iPhone can scan a compatible WiFi QR code displayed on an Android phone and use it to join the network.</p>\n<h3>Why does my WiFi QR code scan but not connect?</h3>\n<p>Common reasons include an incorrect password, wrong security settings, a weak WiFi signal, or an unavailable network.</p>\n<h2>Conclusion</h2>\n<p>Now you know how to scan a WiFi QR code on Android and iPhone. Open your camera, scan the code, and follow the connection prompt to join the network without manually typing the password.</p>\n<p>If you're sharing your own WiFi, create a scannable code using the <a href=\"/wifi-qr-code-generator/\">GenerateQRFast WiFi QR Code Generator</a> and test it before giving it to others.</p>",
